# The Invoice lifecycle, one request at a time: the "Try it" walkthrough in docs/features/invoices.md.
# Works in Rider, Visual Studio and VS Code (REST Client extension). Send the requests in order.
#
# Before the first request:
#   - host: under 'aspire run', copy the api resource's URL from the dashboard; the IDE launch
#     profiles and the dev container serve http://localhost:5171.
#   - credentials: choose the 'dev' environment. Rider and Visual Studio find it in
#     ../http-client.env.json, one folder up so that no build or container image ever copies it.
#     VS Code's REST Client reads environments from its settings instead: copy the 'dev' block there.
#   - tokens and ids: each placeholder below names the response it comes from; paste the value in.
#     Nothing secret is committed: the env file holds the Development seed account, and every token
#     here is minted by your own API and expires after 15 minutes. To chain values instead of
#     pasting them, name a request with '# @name login' and use {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
#     (Visual Studio, VS Code), or set a global from a response handler script (Rider).

@host = http://localhost:5171
@token = paste-accessToken-from-step-1
@invoiceId = paste-id-from-step-2
@etag = paste-ETag-header-from-step-5
@memberToken = paste-accessToken-from-step-10
# Step 8 sends this key again to replay step 2. Change it before a second walk-through: the same key
# keeps answering with the first invoice, paid by then, so steps 3, 4 and 7 would answer 409.
@createKey = try-it-1

### 1. Sign in as the seeded admin (200: accessToken, refreshToken, expiresInSeconds)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2. Create a draft invoice (201: Location header and the new id)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{createKey}}

{
  "customerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "customerEmail": "ada@example.com",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 3. Add a line; only a draft accepts one (204)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/lines
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Analytical engine consulting",
  "amount": 1200.00
}

### 4. Issue it; the due date may not lie in the past (204)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/issue
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dueDate": "2099-12-31T00:00:00Z"
}

### 5. Read it (200: status Issued, total 1200.00, and an ETag header such as W/"812")
GET {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Read it again with that ETag (304, no body: nothing changed)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-None-Match: {{etag}}

### 7. Pay it (204); within seconds the outbox delivers the receipt: watch the api's log
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Replay step 2: same key, same body (201 again, same Location, Idempotency-Replayed: true)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{createKey}}

{
  "customerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "customerEmail": "ada@example.com",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 9. Register a member; Development opens self-registration (200; 409 once the account exists)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{memberEmail}}",
  "password": "{{memberPassword}}"
}

### 10. Sign in as the member (200: accessToken)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{memberEmail}}",
  "password": "{{memberPassword}}"
}

### 11. Try to create an invoice as the member (403 Auth.Forbidden: members hold invoices:read only)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Charles Babbage",
  "customerEmail": "charles@example.com",
  "currency": "EUR"
}
